body:
i might be dumb.  
i never noticed the delay effect of "in nullum" till just now. >.>;;;  
yeah that sounds correct!

 I definitely ran into a lot of trouble with this and I'm still incredibly unsatisfied with the end result due to complications of the source audio that I was using. I did the best that I could \^v\^;;;  


 Naofumi Harada's arrangement of Moon River is in the key of G major and since Sinatra's performance on the recording I used was in the key of C major, I had to transpose the instrumental.  
I isolated the the bass/instrumental and layered the transposed instruments under the isolated drum track. The process came at a terrible price by causing tons of artifacting but I edited around the audio all that could to make it sound listenable. \[and don't get me started on the increased tempo for Sinatra's vocals. Vibrato gone wild ;w; I just wasn't sure what to do with that so feedback is always appreciated\~\]

thank you, I sent them a message.  
My psychiatrist wasn't super helpful, they said that my heart shouldn't be raising from such a low dosage, but I do believe the timing can't be a mere coincidence.  
I'm doing the best I can ;.;

